  <keyword>hysteresis</keyword>
  <keyword_alias>block:hysteresis</keyword_alias>
  <short_description>Relay: latching two-threshold switch (uHigh, uLow, yHigh, yLow).</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>Block type: hysteresis</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <param_input>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>input ports</param_name>
      <param_description>1 input port(s) declared.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
  </param_input>
  <param_output>
    <param_output_item>
      <param_name>output ports</param_name>
      <param_description>1 output port(s) declared.</param_description>
    </param_output_item>
  </param_output>
  <description>
    <p>Relay: a latching switch with two thresholds (hysteresis).</p>
    <table border="1">
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Module</td><td><code>nflow_blocks</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Library</td><td>Nonlinear</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Type</td><td><code>hysteresis</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Label</td><td>Relay</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p><img src="../../../../libraries/nonlinear/exports/hysteresis.svg" align="middle"/></p>
    <p><b>Description</b></p>
    <p>The output latches: it switches to <code>yHigh</code> when the input rises to or above <code>uHigh</code>, to <code>yLow</code> when it falls to or below <code>uLow</code>, and holds its previous value in between. This two-threshold behaviour is the classic relay with hysteresis. Stateful (latched output).</p>
    <p><b>Ports</b></p>
    <table border="1">
      <thead><tr><th>Port</th><th>Role</th><th>Side</th><th>Position</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Port_1</td><td>Control input compared against the thresholds.</td><td>left</td><td>x=0, y=40</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p><b>Output(s)</b></p>
    <table border="1">
      <thead><tr><th>Port</th><th>Role</th><th>Side</th><th>Position</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Port_1</td><td>Latched relay output (yHigh or yLow).</td><td>right</td><td>x=80, y=40</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p><b>Parameters</b></p>
    <table border="1">
      <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Default value</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>uHigh</code></td><td>1</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>uLow</code></td><td>-1</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>yHigh</code></td><td>1</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>yLow</code></td><td>0</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p><b>Block Characteristics</b></p>
    <table border="1">
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Block type</td><td>hysteresis</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Family</td><td>Nonlinear</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Rendered size</td><td>80 x 80</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Phases</td><td>INIT, OUTPUT, UPDATE</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Internal state or history</td><td>yes (latched output)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Signal data type</td><td>double numeric values</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p><b>Algorithms</b></p>
    <ul>
      <li>INIT: start at yLow.</li>
      <li>OUTPUT: emit the latched value.</li>
      <li>UPDATE: switch to yHigh above uHigh, to yLow below uLow, otherwise hold.</li>
    </ul>
    <p><b>Equation or Rule</b></p>
    <latex>y \leftarrow \begin{cases} y_{High} &amp; u \ge u_{High} \\ y_{Low} &amp; u \le u_{Low} \\ y &amp; \text{otherwise} \end{cases}</latex>
    <p><b>Extended Capabilities</b></p>
    <p>Code generation: supported for C and Rust.</p>
